What this establishes, in one line: on every vector the core and the
generated Java codec drop the unrecognised field and protobuf-java carries
it through to the re-encode. Java's incumbent RETAINS, where the rust
slice's (prost) does not, so this is the first direct measurement of the
guarantee ABI v1 open decision 11 would remove rather than an argument
about one. Who it bites is unchanged and specific: a client that decodes
and never re-encodes loses nothing; a worker forwarding a ProcessRequest
between two schema versions loses the field silently.
